; Anomaly Coop - where a player's checkpoint (camp) may come from (F3, docs/CHECKPOINTS_DEATH.md par. 2.2). Merged into
; system.ltx (DLTX); read by the engine on the host (coop_checkpoint_sources.cpp) when a session starts.
;   campfire  - a lit campfire within campfire_radius, stood next to it campfire_dwell_ms and not in a fight
;               (an enemy within combat_radius picked him); a fight restarts the count;
;   tent      - the player's own tent or sleeping bag (objects of tent_sections): he claims "I put one up here"
;               (coop.checkpoint.claim_tent). The host's own is put up by the stock item_tent, and the claim takes the
;               nearest new one within tent_claim_radius. A client's the host puts up itself (tent_section /
;               sleepbag_section), paid with an item of his from the stock lists in item_lists, at most 8 per player;
;               "pack" gives that item back. His tent within tent_rest_radius is also a rest place;
;   rest      - inside a stock sleep zone ([coop_rest_zones]) or a surge cover ([list] of cover_list), when he lies down;
;   mod       - an object a mod declares with coop.checkpoint.register_source(id, radius), as a campfire;
;   base      - Build 57 (owner 2026-11-18: "on any base the respawn must be at the bed, not at the campfire"): a player on
;               the ground of a base of [coop_bases] that is not hostile to him (hostile: it has an owner the game knows
;               and every one of its owners is his enemy; the same level, within its radius and 10 m in height; he leaves
;               it beyond radius + base_leave_margin, or 15 m in height) gets its bed (the sleep zone; kind "rest",
;               "Camp updated: a sleeping place.") as his checkpoint after base_dwell_ms there out of a fight, once. While
;               he is on it, its campfires and mod objects set nothing (and say nothing); lying down on it, or a story
;               checkpoint while he stands on it, writes the bed; his own tent on it stays his checkpoint. A respawn whose
;               bed belongs to a base hostile to him now takes the record before it on his level; without one he comes
;               back as a player without a checkpoint does. A hostile base is no base for him: its campfires work as before.
;               Build 57 (owner 2026-11-18: "for the bases that are not covered, just put the point at the place of the
;               first spawn on that base"; the lead: real bases without a sleeping place, not every start location): a
;               row of [coop_start_bases] is a base too, with the owners of its row, at the point of that start location
;               in base_start_locations, within base_start_radius; its record is kind "rest" without an object ("Camp
;               updated: a base."). Two bases of one level whose ground overlaps are one: the later row is dropped (the
;               log names both). In the Server mode ("in split maps in the console form this must be done too") the map
;               server of the level says on which base's ground a player stands, the world server decides as above.
; A radius is in metres, 0 < r <= 500; a time is in ms, 0..600000 (tent_claim_ms 5000..600000). A value outside falls
; back to the one below; tent_section / sleepbag_section must spawn and be in tent_sections, else clients get none.
; Mod packs change them or add rest zones with DLTX (![coop_checkpoints], ![coop_rest_zones]).

[coop_checkpoints]
campfire_radius   = 3
campfire_dwell_ms = 5000
combat_radius     = 50
tent_sections     = ph_tent, ph_sleepbag
tent_section      = ph_tent       ; put up for a client's tent claim (stock itm_tent placeable_section)
sleepbag_section  = ph_sleepbag   ; put up for a client's sleeping bag claim (stock itm_sleepbag placeable_section)
tent_rest_radius  = 2
tent_claim_radius = 4
tent_claim_ms     = 15000
cover_list        = misc\surge_manager.ltx   ; section [list]: stock surge covers (264)
item_lists        = items\settings\itms_manager.ltx   ; [tent_i_bag_sections], [sleeping_bag_sections]: what pays
base_dwell_ms     = 3000   ; Build 57: on a base this long, not in a fight, and its bed is the checkpoint
base_leave_margin = 10     ; Build 57: once on a base he is on it until its radius + this
base_start_locations = plugins\new_game_start_locations.ltx   ; Build 57: the points of [coop_start_bases] (empty: none)
base_start_radius = 50     ; Build 57: the ground of a start location base

